|~ `::group`, the steps in parentheses run on the value in the pipe, and
   what is declared under it: its constructor and its refusals.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:group
  |~~ A group, `(…)`, runs a pipeline as one word: its steps run on the
      value in the pipe, it answers what its last step answers, and the
      names it declares stay inside. A modifier of more than one word
      stands in one, `take (count | sub 1)`, and the quotes of a template
      `get` runs are forks of their own, `5 | get [~(add 1) ~(mul 2)]`
      answering `[6 10]`.

      In a quote the step is a record that holds the quote of the
      pipeline it stands for, `~((add 1 | mul 2)) | first` answering
      `::group~(add 1 | mul 2)`.
      ::link~(::bind | doc) ::link~(::qlang/pipeline | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The quote of a pipeline, built into the step `(pipeline)`. ~~|
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ The payload of `::group` is the quote of its pipeline, so
            `~(add 1 | mul 2) | tag ::group` is the step
            `(add 1 | mul 2)`.
            ::link~(::group | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadEmptyError
        |~~ A group holds one step at least, and `it` keeps the value as it
            is, `~(it) | tag ::group`.
            ::link~(::group | doc)
        ~~|
    | proves :holdsItsSteps
        |~~ A group holds its steps. ~~|
        ~(~((add 1 | mul 2)) | first | payload | count | eq 2)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(42 | tag ::group !| get [~(type) /actualType] | eq [::group/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::number])
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/buildsTheStepOfAPipeline
        |~~ The quote of a pipeline builds the group that runs it. ~~|
        ~(~(add 1 | mul 2) | tag ::group | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote | eq ~((add 1 | mul 2)))
    | proves :PayloadEmptyError/refusesAnEmptyGroup
        |~~ An empty group holds no step. ~~|
        ~(~() | tag ::group !| type | eq ::group/PayloadEmptyError)
    | proves :PayloadEmptyError/keepsTheValueByIt
        |~~ A group of `it` is a step that keeps the value. ~~|
        ~(~(it) | tag ::group | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote | eq ~((it)))
    | impl ::builtin{}

